    {
      "id": 130320,
      "name": "HappiestMeal",
      "username": "HappiestMeal",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/h/22d042/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-03T05:04:22.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ha! That's awesome.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/grin.png?v=12\" title=\":grin:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":grin:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> How did you get it to show a negative HP?!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'm not sure if the glitch applies either.&nbsp; I had cold snap and AZ's cold damage was buffed by +3.&nbsp; Voss just used Forced Deployment and the envornment let him play a ton of cards.&nbsp; So there was the flagship, the&nbsp;dreadnaught, both Quark Drive thingies, 8+ minions (I remember it was almost enough for the win condition but not quite there), and Voss himself.&nbsp; So I dealt 4 cold to everything just with cold snap, used frost bound drain, and then used Thermal Shockwave for some more cold damage.&nbsp; All in all I did about 70 cold damage in a turn.&nbsp; That's&nbsp;when Thermal Shockwave&nbsp;dealt me 70ish fire damage damage and made me freak out because I forgot it did all cold damage and not just it's own.&nbsp; Now I don't know if this was the glitch or not but then the Isothermic Transducer reacted and before AZ died and let me deal that much damage to a target, so I picked Voss leaving him somewhere in the -20's instantly ending the game.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I don't know if my Isothermic Transducer would have reacted before incap or if it would have just instantly stopped all of AZ's actions and incaped him.&nbsp; It sounds like a glitch to me, honestly.&nbsp; Without a clear rulling, if we were at a table with cards in hand and that happed I would say that it would not have worked, and AZ would be flipped no further damage dealt.&nbsp; I just had to share that photo though, as I thought about what facial expression Voss had, and is stuck with, now that he is trapped in a 20 foot thick wall of ice.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Is it a glitch?&nbsp; Probably.&nbsp; Does anyone know, when AZ does enough to kill himself in fire damage does Isothermic Transducer react or does he flip and lose the Transducer first?&nbsp; Either way it was still amazing.&nbsp; AZ was at like full health right before he took that huge 71 damage hit.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:05:25.323Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
