      "raw": "[quote=\"Rabit\"]\n\nHa! That&#39;s awesome.  :grin: How did you get it to show a negative HP?!\n\n[/quote]\n\nI&#39;m not sure if the glitch applies either.&nbsp; I had cold snap and AZ&#39;s cold damage was buffed by +3.&nbsp; Voss just used Forced Deployment and the envornment let him play a ton of cards.&nbsp; So there was the flagship, the&nbsp;dreadnaught, both Quark Drive thingies, 8+ minions (I remember it was almost enough for the win condition but not quite there), and Voss himself.&nbsp; So I dealt 4 cold to everything just with cold snap, used frost bound drain, and then used Thermal Shockwave for some more cold damage.&nbsp; All in all I did about 70 cold damage in a turn.&nbsp; That&#39;s&nbsp;when Thermal Shockwave&nbsp;dealt me 70ish fire damage damage and made me freak out because I forgot it did all cold damage and not just it&#39;s own.&nbsp; Now I don&#39;t know if this was the glitch or not but then the Isothermic Transducer reacted and before AZ died and let me deal that much damage to a target, so I picked Voss leaving him somewhere in the -20&#39;s instantly ending the game.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nI don&#39;t know if my Isothermic Transducer would have reacted before incap or if it would have just instantly stopped all of AZ&#39;s actions and incaped him.&nbsp; It sounds like a glitch to me, honestly.&nbsp; Without a clear rulling, if we were at a table with cards in hand and that happed I would say that it would not have worked, and AZ would be flipped no further damage dealt.&nbsp; I just had to share that photo though, as I thought about what facial expression Voss had, and is stuck with, now that he is trapped in a 20 foot thick wall of ice.\n\n&nbsp;\n\nIs it a glitch?&nbsp; Probably.&nbsp; Does anyone know, when AZ does enough to kill himself in fire damage does Isothermic Transducer react or does he flip and lose the Transducer first?&nbsp; Either way it was still amazing.&nbsp; AZ was at like full health right before he took that huge 71 damage hit.\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;\n\n&nbsp;",
